IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja3-sch3-third-schedule.l4: the Third Schedule of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore),
-- 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024 (plain-text rendering SCJA1969.txt, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, written from the text alone.  Answers seam 3 of PLAN.md (the asking section is s 21(1)(b), in scja1's range).
-- A result is MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Schedule itself gives, NOTHING means it does not answer.

§ `Third Schedule: orders of a District Court or Magistrate's Court that are appealable only with permission`

-- Helper used by the four limbs below: one answer from several limbs.  Any limb that holds gives JUST TRUE.
-- Limbs that all fail give JUST FALSE, because s 21(1)(b) hands "any case specified in the Third Schedule" to this list of four.
-- A limb that cannot be answered leaves the whole NOTHING.
GIVEN limbs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 the limbs taken together` MEANS
    IF elem (JUST TRUE) limbs
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF elem NOTHING limbs
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any of the following cases" [handed to a list, and no head in the list holds; delegated-definition ruling (a) of 2026-11-05]
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- A decision of a District Court or Magistrate's Court (the Schedule's own scope: "a decision of a District Court or Magistrate's Court").
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 3 the decision is one of a District Court or Magistrate's Court` MEANS
    decision's `made by` EQUALS `District Court` OR decision's `made by` EQUALS `Magistrate's Court`

-- src:5802 | (a) where a District Court or Magistrate’s Court makes an order giving
-- src:5803 | unconditional permission to defend any proceedings;
@ref Third Schedule case (a) (src:5802-5803)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 case (a) the order gives unconditional permission to defend` MEANS
    IF `sch 3 the decision is one of a District Court or Magistrate's Court` decision
       AND decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `permission to defend proceedings`
       AND decision's `the order`'s `way it went` EQUALS `granted unconditionally`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a District Court or Magistrate’s Court makes an order giving unconditional permission to defend any proceedings"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5807 | (b) where a District Court or Magistrate’s Court makes an order giving
-- src:5808 | permission to defend any proceedings on condition that the party
-- src:5809 | defending those proceedings pays into court or gives security for the
-- src:5810 | sum claimed, except if the appellant is that party;
@ref Third Schedule case (b) (src:5807-5810)
-- "except if the appellant is that party": the party defending is the one who must pay into court or give security.
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      `the appellant is the party defending those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appellant the party who is defending, and who must pay into court or give security for the sum claimed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 case (b) the order gives permission to defend on condition of payment into court or security` MEANS
    IF `sch 3 the decision is one of a District Court or Magistrate's Court` decision
       AND decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `permission to defend proceedings`
       AND decision's `the order`'s `way it went` EQUALS `granted on condition that the party pays into court or gives security for the sum claimed`
       AND (NOT `the appellant is the party defending those proceedings`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where ... on condition that the party defending those proceedings pays into court or gives security for the sum claimed, except if the appellant is that party"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5814 | (c) where a District Court or Magistrate’s Court makes an order setting
-- src:5815 | aside unconditionally a default judgment, regardless of how the default
-- src:5816 | judgment was obtained (including whether by reason of a breach of an
-- src:5817 | order of court or otherwise);
@ref Third Schedule case (c) (src:5814-5817)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 case (c) the order sets aside a default judgment unconditionally` MEANS
    IF `sch 3 the decision is one of a District Court or Magistrate's Court` decision
       AND decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `setting aside a default judgment`
       AND decision's `the order`'s `way it went` EQUALS `granted unconditionally`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a District Court or Magistrate’s Court makes an order setting aside unconditionally a default judgment, regardless of how the default judgment was obtained"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5819 | (d) where a District Court or Magistrate’s Court makes an order setting
-- src:5820 | aside a default judgment on condition that the party against whom the
-- src:5821 | judgment had been entered pays into court or gives security for the sum
-- src:5822 | claimed, regardless of how the default judgment was obtained
-- src:5823 | (including whether by reason of a breach of an order of court or
-- src:5824 | otherwise), except if the appellant is that party.
@ref Third Schedule case (d) (src:5819-5824)
-- "except if the appellant is that party": the party against whom the default judgment had been entered.
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      `the appellant is the party against whom the default judgment had been entered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appellant the party against whom the default judgment had been entered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 case (d) the order sets aside a default judgment on condition of payment into court or security` MEANS
    IF `sch 3 the decision is one of a District Court or Magistrate's Court` decision
       AND decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `setting aside a default judgment`
       AND decision's `the order`'s `way it went` EQUALS `granted on condition that the party pays into court or gives security for the sum claimed`
       AND (NOT `the appellant is the party against whom the default judgment had been entered`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a District Court or Magistrate’s Court makes an order setting aside a default judgment on condition that the party against whom the judgment had been entered pays into court or gives security for the sum claimed ... except if the appellant is that party"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5791 | An appeal lies to the General Division from a decision of a District Court or
-- src:5792 | Magistrate’s Court only with the permission of that District Court or Magistrate’s
-- src:5793 | Court or the General Division in any of the following cases:
@ref Third Schedule (opening words) (src:5791-5793)
-- Seam 3 of PLAN.md.  The two "appellant is that party" facts are one fact in the long form of the question: the appellant is the party who
-- must pay into court or give security (case (b)), or the party against whom the default judgment had been entered (case (d)).
-- The Schedule says what is specified; it does not say what follows for a case it does not specify, so the question here is membership.
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      `the appellant is the party defending those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appellant the party who is defending, and who must pay into court or give security for the sum claimed?
      `the appellant is the party against whom the default judgment had been entered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appellant the party against whom the default judgment had been entered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` MEANS
    IF `sch 3 the decision is one of a District Court or Magistrate's Court` decision
    THEN `sch 3 the limbs taken together` (LIST
             `sch 3 case (a) the order gives unconditional permission to defend` decision
           , `sch 3 case (b) the order gives permission to defend on condition of payment into court or security` decision `the appellant is the party defending those proceedings`
           , `sch 3 case (c) the order sets aside a default judgment unconditionally` decision
           , `sch 3 case (d) the order sets aside a default judgment on condition of payment into court or security` decision `the appellant is the party against whom the default judgment had been entered`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Schedule speaks of "a decision of a District Court or Magistrate’s Court"; a decision of another court is outside its scope
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:5791 | An appeal lies to the General Division from a decision of a District Court or
-- src:5792 | Magistrate’s Court only with the permission of that District Court or Magistrate’s
-- src:5793 | Court or the General Division in any of the following cases:
@ref Third Schedule (opening words) (src:5791-5793)
-- The Schedule's effect: in a case it specifies, an appeal lies to the General Division "only with the permission of that District Court
-- or Magistrate's Court or the General Division".  Which of the two gives permission is the person's choice of whom to ask, so the court is not computed.
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      `the appellant is the party defending those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appellant the party who is defending, and who must pay into court or give security for the sum claimed?
      `the appellant is the party against whom the default judgment had been entered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appellant the party against whom the default judgment had been entered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 an appeal lies only with permission of that court or the General Division` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 3 the decision is a case specified in the Third Schedule` decision `the appellant is the party defending those proceedings` `the appellant is the party against whom the default judgment had been entered`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Schedule says an appeal lies "only with the permission" in the cases it lists; for a decision it does not list it says nothing either way
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a decision of a court the Schedule does not speak of
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
